accionAyuda,Help
tituloAyuda,IoT help
textoAyuda,Tool for classes with a DP. Every class inheriting from IotDpObject has a DPT with its decorated properties.
tituloSinGuardar,Unsaved file
textoSinGuardar,The editor has unsaved changes. Save the file and generate again. Nothing has been changed.
textoGuardar,The //@generado block has been rewritten in the editor: save the file.
ayuda01,DECORATORS
ayuda02,  //@dp:<path> opens a block and //@end closes it. Empty path = DP root; levels with dots: //@dp:estado.velocidad
ayuda03,  Inside a block only 'protected type name;' (no initializer). Blocks are not nested.
ayuda04,  protected: IotDpObject is in another library and can only see the child properties this way.
ayuda05,  Types: bool int uint float string time langString, their dyn_ and mapping (stored as JSON).
ayuda06,INHERITANCE
ayuda07,  class B : A with #uses of A. The DPT of B has what A has plus its own; generating A regenerates all its descendants.
ayuda08,DP ACCESS
ayuda09,  Properties hold no values: every get reads the DP at that moment and every set writes it immediately.
ayuda10,  Getters and setters generated in the //@generado block: getVelocidad() and setVelocidad(value). Do not edit them by hand.
ayuda11,  Several at once: getVarios(makeDynString("run", "actual"), values) and setVarios(makeMapping("run", true)).
ayuda12,  Usage: shared_ptr<IotMotor> m = new IotMotor("motor1"); m.setRun(true);
ayuda13,STEPS
ayuda14,  1. Save the class. 2. IoT > Generate DPT from class (Ctrl+Shift+G). 3. Save again (the //@generado block is written in the editor).
exploradorEditar,Edit
